(A) Binary Classification 

Examples:
Spam vs Not Spam
Disease vs No Disease

Best Algorithms:
Logistic Regression (baseline)
Random Forest ⭐
XGBoost / LightGBM ⭐⭐⭐ (very strong)
SVM (small-medium data)
Neural Networks (large data)

(B) Multi-class Classification

Examples:
Digit recognition (0–9)
Product category prediction

Best Algorithms:
Logistic Regression (multinomial)
Random Forest
XGBoost / LightGBM ⭐⭐⭐
Neural Networks (CNN for images)


(C) Multi-label Classification

👉 One sample → multiple labels

Example:
Movie → [Action, Comedy]

Best Algorithms:
Binary Relevance (multiple logistic models)
Random Forest
Neural Networks ⭐


(D) Imbalanced Classification ⚠️ (VERY IMPORTANT in real world)
👉 One class dominates

Example:
Fraud detection (99% normal, 1% fraud)

Problems:
Model predicts majority only

Solutions + Algorithms:
XGBoost (handles imbalance well) ⭐
Random Forest

Use:
SMOTE
Class weights
Precision/Recall instead of accuracy

